CODE REVIEW REQUEST: Work-session overlap check

BACKGROUND AND EXPECTED BEHAVIOUR
A scheduling utility receives work sessions represented by dictionaries with start and end values measured in minutes from the beginning of a day. A session must finish after it begins. The result should report whether any accepted sessions overlap, with touching endpoints allowed. Input sessions may arrive in any order and must not be rearranged in place, because the caller also uses their original order for display. An empty collection is valid and has no overlap. If an invalid interval is present, validation should fail before an overlap result is returned. The following utility is local and has no calendar-service dependency.

IMPLEMENTATION SUPPLIED FOR REVIEW
```python
def has_conflict(sessions):
    sessions.sort(key=lambda row: row["start"])
    previous = None
    for session in sessions:
        start = session["start"]
        end = session["end"]
        if previous is not None and start <= previous:
            return True
        if end < start:
            raise ValueError("invalid interval")
        previous = end
    return False

