BACKGROUND AND EXPECTED BEHAVIOUR
A local reporting function groups expense amounts by currency. Amounts are represented as decimal strings so exact decimal arithmetic is possible. Different currencies must never be added into a single monetary total. Unknown currency codes should remain separate groups rather than be silently converted. The caller needs totals suitable for display with the currency attached, and the original expense entries must remain unchanged. The records below are fictional administrative data; the task does not require exchange rates or access to payment systems. Examine whether the prototype respects the stated representation and grouping requirements.

